^SAMPLE = GSM9814812
!Sample_title = MAPS
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9814812
!Sample_status = Public on Jul 10 2026
!Sample_submission_date = Jun 15 2026
!Sample_last_update_date = Jul 10 2026
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = ipsilateral brain hemisphere
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: ipsilateral brain hemisphere
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: Wild type
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: Stroke+MAPS
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Mice subjected to ischemic stroke received implantation of different hydrogel microsphere formulations into the infarct cavity at 5 days post-stroke. At day 14 after stroke, ipsilateral hemispheres were harvested for single-cell RNA sequencing analysis. Healthy control mice received no treatment.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Brain tissues were immediately collected and washed twice with cold RNase-free PBS. Samples were minced and enzymatically dissociated in digestion buffer containing Collagenase IV, Papain, and DNase I for 20 min at 37 °C. Enzymatic digestion was terminated with PBS supplemented with 10% FBS, followed by mechanical trituration. Cell suspensions were filtered through 70 µm and 30 µm strainers. Red blood cells and dead cells were removed using erythrocyte lysis buffer and Dead Cell Removal MicroBeads (MACS), respectively. Live cells were washed and resuspended in PBS containing 0.04% BSA. Only cell suspensions with viability greater than 85% were used for downstream library preparation.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Single-cell suspensions were loaded onto Chromium Single Cell 3′ Chips (10x Genomics, v3) targeting approximately 8,000 cells per sample. Single-cell barcoding, reverse transcription, cDNA amplification, and library construction were performed according to the manufacturer's instructions. Libraries were sequenced on an Illumina NovaSeq 6000 platform using paired-end 150 bp sequencing.
!Sample_description = Library name: SAMPLES1
!Sample_description = Single-cell transcriptomic profiling of dissociated cells isolated from the ipsilateral hemisphere at 14 days after ischemic stroke following implantation of MAPS at day 5 post-stroke.
!Sample_data_processing = Raw BCL files were converted to FASTQ format using bcl2fastq (v5.0.1).
!Sample_data_processing = FASTQ files were processed using Cell Ranger (v7.0.0) for read alignment, barcode assignment, UMI counting, and generation of gene-cell count matrices.
!Sample_data_processing = Gene expression matrices were imported into Seurat (v4.1.0) for quality control. Cells expressing fewer than 500 genes or containing more than 25% mitochondrial transcripts were excluded.
!Sample_data_processing = Expression data were normalized using LogNormalize. Highly variable genes were selected for dimensionality reduction and clustering. PCA was performed and the top 20 principal components were used for graph-based clustering and UMAP visualization.
!Sample_data_processing = Cell-type annotation was performed using marker genes and reference databases including SingleR, scCATCH, and LC-Marker. Functional enrichment, AUCell scoring, and cell-cell communication analyses were subsequently conducted.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: GRCm39
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Processed data include filtered gene-cell UMI count matrices generated by Cell Ranger and used for downstream analyses.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24247
!Sample_contact_name = Mengying,,An
